course: dictionary
lesson: 16152
title: Wintry: cold, icy or unfriendly
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word wintry comes from winter, so it means like winter. When you meet it, look at the words around it. Words like snow, frost, ice or coats are clues that tell you the meaning.
explain: «The wintry wind bit at our cheeks as we walked to school.» A wind that bites your cheeks is cold, so wintry means cold and wintry weather is like winter weather.
explain: «She gave me a wintry smile and turned away.» A smile cannot be snowy or icy, so the clue is that she turned away. Try the meaning in the sentence: a cold, unfriendly smile fits, so wintry describes a manner that is not warm.
fact: Wintry means typical of winter: cold, snowy, icy or frosty.
fact: «Wintry» can also describe a smile or a manner that is cold and unfriendly.
fact: In UK weather forecasts, «wintry showers» means showers of rain mixed with sleet or snow.
fact: Wintry is an adjective, so it describes a noun, such as «wintry weather» or «a wintry scene».
exercise: What does wintry mean? | Brand new and shiny | Hot and sunny | Very noisy and busy | *Cold, snowy, icy or frosty
exercise: In a weather forecast, which phrase means rain mixed with sleet or snow? | gentle fog | *wintry showers | sunny spells | warm breezes
exercise: «Her wintry smile showed she did not want to be friends.» What does wintry suggest about the smile? | *Cold and unfriendly | Bright and funny | Loud and cheerful | Warm and welcoming
test: «We wrapped up warmly for the wintry weather.» Why did they wrap up warmly? | *To keep warm in the cold, icy weather | To look fashionable at a party | To hide from the bright sun | To go swimming in the lake
test: Which word is closest in meaning to wintry when it describes a cold, unfriendly manner? | loud | *cold | sunny | gentle
exam: Which sentence uses wintry to mean cold and unfriendly? | We ate ice cream in the wintry sunshine | *Her wintry stare made me feel unwelcome | The wintry showers made the garden grow | The children built a snowman in the wintry park
